    "author": "lojeevlim",
    "email": "lojeevlim@gmail.com",
    "subject": "Add Feedback components, fix classNames Web Component support, normalize code examples",
    "body": "- Build out the \"Feedback\" section: Alert, Toast, Notification, ProgressBar,\nEmptyState, ErrorState, SuccessState, and LoadingState, each with a full\nReact component, Web Component registration, showcase, and Playground.\nThe four \"*State\" components share a small internal StatusLayout helper.\n- Register `classNames` (and `className` where missing) as a real \"json\"/\n\"string\" Web Component prop on Modal, Button, Alert, Accordion/\nAccordionItem, List/ListItem, and Breadcrumbs/BreadcrumbItem — previously\nthese were React-only, so every \"Custom styling\" example showed a fallback\nnote instead of real js/vue/angular code. Now `el.classNames = {...}` /\n`:classNames` / `[classNames]` genuinely work at runtime.\n- Add a named `slot=\"content\"` to Popover for rich (non-string) content,\nenabling its \"Rich content\" example to work as a Web Component.\n- Simplify Table's custom-render example to return a plain string instead of\nJSX in the non-React variants, since a React element can't cross into a\nWeb Component property (same precedent as Tabs/Carousel).\n- Normalize every remaining code example: dash-cased attribute names\n(`default-open`, `icon-only`, `show-value`, etc.) renamed to their camelCase\nReact prop names, and boolean attributes written as explicit `=\"true\"`\nconverted to bare shorthand — matching the React variant's style exactly\nacross all four languages."
